  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Evaluating a Limit Near a Point</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Find \(\displaystyle \lim_{x \rightarrow {@point@}} {@fx@}\).</p><p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>Given the expression:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 30px">\(\displaystyle \lim_{x \rightarrow {@point@}} {@fx@}\).</p>
<p>To find the limit of the above expression, we first need to simplify it;</p>

<p style="margin-left: 30px">\(\displaystyle \lim_{x \rightarrow {@point@}} {@fx@} = \lim_{{x \rightarrow {@point@}}} \frac{({@x - aa@})({@x - aa@})}{({@x - aa@})}= \lim_{{x \rightarrow {@point@}}} ({@x - aa@})\). <p>

<p>Now, we can directly evaluate the limit by plugging in the value of \(x\), which is \({@point@}\).</p>

<p style="margin-left: 30px">\(\lim_{{x \to {@point@}}} ({@x - aa@}) = {@point@}{@sign_ev@}{@ev(abs(aa),simp)@} = {@ta@}\) </p>

<p>Therefore,</p>

<p style="margin-left: 30px">\(\displaystyle \lim_{{x \rightarrow {@point@}}} \frac{{({@x - aa@})^2}}{{{@x - aa@}}} = {@ta@}\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
